⚠  requires_human = true  A human must review this plan before code generation 
proceeds.

Goal
Fix the requests Session so that environment variables REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE and 
CURL_CA_BUNDLE are ignored when self.verify is explicitly set to False, by 
resolving None verify kwargs against self.verify before checking environment CA 
bundles.

Files to modify
  • src/requests/sessions.py

Implementation steps
  1. Step 1: In src/requests/sessions.py, modify 
Session.merge_environment_settings. Immediately before the existing block that 
checks verify is True or verify is None against the environment CA bundles, add 
an assignment: if verify is None: verify = self.verify. This ensures the 
session-level verify setting is consulted before the environment override logic 
runs.
  2. Step 2: In src/requests/sessions.py, update the existing environment CA 
bundle check inside merge_environment_settings to only apply env bundles when 
verify is True or None (keeping the existing condition, which now correctly 
skips application when verify is False or a string path).
  3. Step 3: Add a unit test in tests/test_requests.py that creates a Session 
with verify=False, sets the REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE environment variable to an 
invalid path, and asserts that making a request does not raise an exception 
related to the invalid CA bundle path.

Tests to run
  $ pytest tests/test_requests.py

Risks
  ⚠  There is a small risk that downstream code relies on the current behavior 
where a session with verify=None (default) and REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE set would 
still apply the env bundle even if session.verify were later mutated to False, 
though this is exactly the bug being fixed.

